    "result_text": "All green. Here's what I implemented.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds per-country national-number length validation to the E.164 telephone canonicalizer, folded into the single source of truth `E164Telephone.toE164OrNull` (used by both `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` on create and `RejectDuplicateOwnerTelephone` for dedup). A wrong length yields `null`, which `NormalizeOwnerTelephone` already turns into a checked `InvalidTelephoneException` \u2192 **400** \u2014 so no pipeline/handler/DTO wiring changed.\n\n**`E164Telephone.java`** \u2014 added a `country code \u2192 national digit count` table (`\"61\"\u21929`, `\"1\"\u219210`, longest-first) and a `nationalLengthMatchesCountry` check. When a number carries an **explicit** country code (leading `+`), its national-number length must exactly match that country; codes outside the table fall through to the existing generic 8\u201315 bound (so the docstring's `+64` example still validates).\n\n**Scoping decision \u2014 why explicit country codes only:** the normalizer's default path prepends `+61` to bare local numbers. The existing (immovable) `OwnerRestControllerV1Tests.createOwnerSuccess` POSTs `\"6085550000\"` \u2014 a 10-digit local number that defaults to `+61` with 10 national digits and must remain a 201. A uniform \"+61 needs 9\" rule would break it. Keying the exact-length rule off an explicitly-provided country code (what \"the E.164 telephone's country code\" naturally refers to) rejects `\"+61 123\"` (\u2192 400, the new acceptance test) while leaving the inferred-country guess on its generic bound.\n\nAlso refreshed the now-accurate javadoc/message on `InvalidTelephoneException`, `NormalizeOwnerTelephone`, and the `telephone` description in `openapi.yml`.\n\n**Tests:** full suite green \u2014 **255 passed, 0 failures/errors**, including the new `AcceptanceTest.errorRejectsWrongNationalLength` and the entire existing owner/pet/visit/repository suites.",
